        "notes": "One nominal NTA/ferric-chloride input recipe shared by NBRC1020/824 and JCM284. The ten dry amounts in components are exact batch masses expressed in grams, not final concentrations. NBRC prints four of these inputs in milligrams (Co 24 mg, Cu 25 mg, boric acid 10 mg, molybdate 24 mg), exactly normalized in the original proposal to 0.024/0.025/0.01/0.024 g; original source units remain in the bound literal-source profiles. Water and KOH are globally unquantified. NBRC1020/824 list distilled water 1 L and first dissolve NTA in 200 mL water, adjusting that initial solution to pH 6.5 with KOH; the 200 mL is within the listed preparation water. NBRC does not specify final stock pH or an explicit final-volume instruction. JCM284 first dissolves NTA in 200 mL water with KOH to pH 6.5, adds remaining salts, makes the final volume 1.0 L, then readjusts to pH 7.0 with KOH. Only JCM establishes final 1 L/pH 7.0. No 1.2 L water, fixed KOH amount/strength, common final concentration, equal final pH or post-reaction species is asserted. COMPLETE describes the twelve explicitly named immediate inputs (ten dry substances, distilled water, KOH), not analytical speciation. The separate vitamin and Se/W preparations remain excluded. Original RECIPE_TRANSCRIPTION assertions and their distinct source scopes are preserved in the following origin profiles and immutable originals."
