        "method": "CURATED_INTERPRETATION",
        "completeness": "PARTIAL",
        "notes": "This is an ingredient/mixture has-part assertion, not an identity mapping, variant hierarchy, or complete culturing recipe. Follow-on scope: The authentic imported label names meatgranules in FAB, not a whole Oxoid cooked-meat medium. Primary EOLabs overlay and Acumedia granule documentation show broth/material separation and that granules can themselves be formulated products. Neogen and DSMZ/Oxoid FAB recipes differ; no source link selects either for this MicrobeDecoder owner. Retain named meatgranules without guessing tissue, cookingstate, productcatalog or FOODON skeletal-food identity. The other inherited peptone,starch,glucose parts are not newly approved; the current Neogen comparator lacks starch/glucose and cannot retrospectively select the unspecified original formula. Successor dependency assessment: The original Falsen 2005 methods/results text associates Fastidious Anaerobe Broth with Oxoid. Its separately named Anaerobe Systems peptone/yeast/glucose fermentation broth is a different preparation and supplies no FAB recipe. The Neogen NCM0199 sheet is a LabM/Neogen product comparator, unselected for this source. Original Oxoid catalogue/formula and the historical peptone material remain unresolved. The existing meat-granule withdrawal is retained; starch/glucose and other inherited component claims are unchanged and remain unverified. No claim that peptone is absent is made. Withdraw the unsupported peptone component_id and set reference_scope UNMAPPED; retain its existing component_name as historical interpretation, not a newly observed expanded source label. The original assertion method and UNKNOWN/PARTIAL completeness remain unchanged. This is a bounded part-reference correction only. Whole-owner identity, raw labels, occurrence counts, quantities, unrelated components, all historical evidence and source/role/export holds are preserved. Historical all-components-identified statements describe prior states, not a new approval. No new