        "method": "RECIPE_TRANSCRIPTION",
        "completeness": "COMPLETE",
        "notes": "Both complete NBRC 1308 and NBRC 1356 primary tables define this one nominal stock: the same 13 specified solutes, 1 L distilled-water input, and NTA-first preparation, adjusted to pH 6.5 with NaOH before minerals are added, with final pH 7.0 stated. Recipe accession, footnote count and metadata encoding do not define distinct substances. Quantities are literal batch inputs, not G_PER_L concentrations: the sources list 1 L water, without an explicit make-up-to-final-volume instruction. NaOH amount/concentration are unstated. Final pH 7.0 is a stated condition, not an instruction for a second titration or evidence of an additional reagent. COMPLETE describes the fifteen named inputs in the complete cited preparation (thirteen specified solutes, distilled water and NaOH); it does not imply complete quantities, specified NaOH form/concentration, final volume, or final equilibrium species. Unspecified hydrate forms and final equilibrium species are not inferred. Occurrence context stays distinct: CultureMech:007471 ingredients/8 (NBRC 1308; raw Trace element solution**) uses 1 ml and autoclaves the receiving mixture containing this stock under N2/CO2 80/20; CultureMech:007474 ingredients/6 (NBRC 1356; raw Trace element solution****) uses 10 ml filter-sterile stock in the separately prepared N2-handled medium. This nominal formulation identity does not assert identical post-processing endpoints. Case19 NBRC 1020 and 824 occurrences remain assigned to their different reviewed NTA/KOH stock, with its separate Se/W supplement excluded. Raw starred labels are local occurrence provenance only, never global resolving synonyms. Proposal ancestry is preserved unchanged at commit d5a7613c931d45d057eaca7b5ec15280aca76c9e: A-P-NBRC1308-TRACE by /root/research_a and C-P-NBRC1356-TRACE by /root/research_c, with exact old payload/history/review bindings in successor-v2/lineage.json. This successor is authored by /root; neither old uninstalled identifier is installed, merged, or turned into an active alias. No source, owner or export release approval follows."
